2026-08-27T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-1152) 'background removal
 # tags: rfd:feature, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD1152  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-27T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-1152) 'Background removal uses a photo-trained matting model, not a union of part masks.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD1152  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-27T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-1152) 'The union of See-Through's nineteen part masks looks like an obvious foreground matte. On a cosplay photograph it put a real Santa hat in the background and deleted it.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD1152  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-27T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-1152) 'Adopt `ZhengPeng7/BiRefNet_HR-matting` as the default background remover, and use See-Through part masks only as regions, never as labels.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD1152  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-27T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-1152) 'Background removal for photographic corpora
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD1152  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-27T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-1152) 'Background removal uses a photo-trained dichotomous matting model, not a union of semantic part masks. `ZhengPeng7/BiRefNet_HR-matting` is the default. It has no vocabulary to fall outside of, so it cannot lose a garment for not knowing what the garment is.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD1152  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-27T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-1152) 'See-Through is retained for what transfers (geometry) and not for what does not (semantics). Its part masks may be used as regions, never as labels for what covers what.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD1152  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-27T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-1152) '`DETAILS.md` carries the ground-truth ranking and the dtype it depends on.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD1152  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-27T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-1152) 'RFD66606-1006 covers layer decomposition. RFD66606-1153 covers how the resulting mattes are judged. RFD66606-1030 records the See-Through components.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD1152  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-27T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-1152) 'Why the union of part masks fails
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1152  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-27T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-1152) 'It is the wrong instrument for a photographic corpus, for a structural reason rather than a quality one. A union of semantic classes can only keep what it can name, and the model is trained on anime characters. Measured on a cosplay photograph, a Santa hat scored -8.38 on `headwear` (a confident negative, not a borderline miss), so the union placed a real garment in the background and deleted it. No threshold recovers it; at a threshold low enough to matter the union grows from 0.50 to 0.56 of the frame while `headwear` stays empty.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1152  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-27T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-1152) 'The same measurement showed the clothing classes fire on body region rather than on cloth: a nude torso is labelled `topwear`, and mask-derived coverage reads 0.81 to 0.93 on images that are largely bare skin.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1152  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-27T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-1152) 'Why a matting model rather than a segmenter
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1152  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-27T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-1152) 'A dichotomous segmenter is trained against binary ground truth, so its only soft pixels are silhouette antialiasing; a veil comes back either fully kept or fully cut. A matting model is trained against real alpha, so partial transparency is a value it can express.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1152  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-27T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-1152) 'The scale-free test is soft-alpha pixels per pixel of silhouette perimeter. Antialiasing is a constant band along the outline, so it stays near 1 whatever the subject. Transparency is area with no perimeter to pay for it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1152  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-27T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-1152) 'Six photographs chosen for sheer fabric, specular surfaces and wispy hair:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1152  1 LINE
 Text:Written

